    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d227">

                <pb facs="0599" n="567" xml:id="pg567"/>

                <head>227. Memorandum From the Chairman of the Joint Chiefs of Staff (Lemnitzer) to
                    Secretary of Defense McNamara<anchor n="0" xml:id="d227-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">CM-224-61</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1961-06-08">June 8, 1961</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Cuba</item>
                </list>
                <p>In response to your request, the Director for Intelligence, Joint Staff, in
                    consultation with the Central Intelligence Agency, has prepared an estimate of
                    usable guerrilla areas, the political-police control mechanism, key pro-Castro
                    sub-leaders, and possible guerrilla centers in Cuba, enclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>L.L. Lemnitzer<anchor n="1" xml:id="d227-f2"/></p>


                <xi:include href="d227-a1.xml" xpointer="d227-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d227-f1" n="0" type="source" xml:id="d227-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Washington National Records Center, RG 330, OASD (C) Files: FRC 71 A
                    2896, Cuba 381 (Sensitive). Top Secret. A note on the source text indicates that
                    McNamaraʼs office received the memorandum on June 9.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d227-f2" n="1" xml:id="d227-f2-content">
                <p>Printed from a copy that indicates Lemnitzer signed the original.</p>
            </note>
